35,2,1,talk,Servas,,"The pattern is clear. Broad mandates fail; narrow, owned tools survive. We must choose the latter.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Daisuke,,"I found the capital line is frozen, but the software allowance has room. We can fund a small tool without new capital.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Sakura,,Whoa! Half the plants have no signal! And licences cost more than fixed fees? That is a trap!,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,The logs show eleven misroutes from duplicate addresses. Copying records wastes an hour daily. This is a data hygiene issue.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Asuka,,The developers are gone until Q3. The coordination group is two people doing everything by hand. We cannot add more work.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Servas,,"Daisuke, your finding aligns with my own. The software allowance is the path.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Daisuke,,I am relieved. It means we do not need to ask for new money. That feels much less risky.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Sakura,,"If the signal is bad, how do we even test the app? I am worried about the field work.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,The misroutes are not about signal. They are about conflicting data. A single source of truth would fix it.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"If we build a tool, who maintains it? The two people in the coordination group are already drowning.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Servas,,"Asuka, the maintenance burden is real. But a narrow tool for one trade, as my research shows, is easier to sustain.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Daisuke,,I agree. A small tool for one specific problem is easier to manage. I feel better about this direction.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Sakura,,I like the idea of a small tool! But we need to make sure the field techs can actually use it.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,The data loss is the core problem. A tool that standardizes the address entry would stop the misroutes.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Asuka,,"If the tool is simple enough, the two people can handle it. But it must be simple.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Servas,,"We have the budget, the need, and the evidence. Let us move to the candidates.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Daisuke,,I am ready. I hope we choose the one that is most sustainable.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Sakura,,I am excited! Let's see what the candidates are.,"{""words"":9,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Ryuji,,I will evaluate them based on their ability to reduce the daily friction.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Asuka,,I will evaluate them based on whether they add to the existing workload or reduce it.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
