60,3,1,talk,Servas,,Option A addresses the root cause. It creates the single source of truth that prevents the misroutes Ryuji identified.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Daisuke,,"Option A seems to fit the software allowance. It is a data tool, not a new capital project. I feel it is the safest choice.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Sakura,,"Option D sounds fun, but if the signal is bad, it might not work. Option A feels more solid.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Ryuji,,Option A directly targets the duplicate address problem. It reduces the copying time and the misroutes. It is the logical choice.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Asuka,,"Option A requires someone to maintain the catalog. If the coordination group is already overwhelmed, this adds to their burden.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Servas,,"Asuka, the maintenance of a data catalog is less demanding than building a new app. It is a stewardship role, not a development one.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Daisuke,,"I agree with Servas. It is just managing data, not writing code. That should be manageable for the current staff.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Sakura,,I hope it is easy to use! I don't want the techs to get confused by a new system.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Ryuji,,"The data entry is the bottleneck. A shared catalog with review procedures ensures accuracy. It is a process improvement, not just a tool.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Asuka,,"If the review procedures are clear, the workload is distributed. It is not just on the coordination group.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Servas,,"The pattern from the past shows that narrow, owned tools survive. Option A is a narrow tool for a specific problem.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Daisuke,,"I am convinced. It fits the budget, it solves the problem, and it is sustainable. I will vote for A.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Sakura,,I like the idea of everyone having the same information! It feels fair. I will vote for A too.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Ryuji,,The evidence supports A. It addresses the daily losses directly. I will vote for A.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Asuka,,It is the only option that does not require new developers. It is the only one that fits the current staffing reality. I will vote for A.,"{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Servas,,We are in agreement. The past has taught us to choose the sustainable path.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Daisuke,,I feel much better now. We made a careful choice.,"{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Sakura,,Yay! We did it together! I hope it works well.,"{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Ryuji,,The decision is based on reason and evidence. It is the correct one.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Asuka,,It is the only choice that respects the limits of our people.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
